# A Claude Code user relying on an installed plugin (rubber-ducky, from
# ~/.claude/plugins, which contributes skills). Real HOME on purpose, read
# only: kiln reads the same installed_plugins.json and enabledPlugins
# Claude Code writes, and must never write them.
@real
@size 140x45
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/ext-plugins

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SEND /plugin
WAIT 1
SHOT plugin-command
EXPECT /rubber-ducky@apato-plugins/
EXPECT_NOT /\(s\)|vunknown/
TYPE /rubber
WAIT 1
SHOT slash-palette
EXPECT /rubber-ducky:/
KEY backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace
TURN Use the rubber-duck skill to help me think through why our CI flakes about 1 in 20 runs (see notes.txt). Do not change any files, just talk it through.
SHOT rubber-duck-attempt
EXPECT /skill ─+/
EXPECT /loaded · \d+ lines/
